Runs 1 to 3 (acme/lib, max-age 60, ETag "e1"; the meta of the copy is dated 1792065600 by fx/mtimes): 1 miss, one request with no If-None-Match and no Authorization, one write (body, then meta). 2 age 30 s: no request. 3 age 90 s: one request with If-None-Match, the fake answers 304, the result is the copy as status 200, one write of the meta only (the age starts again).
Run 4 (newest, R-AP43 case 1): no list_dirs and no read_files, one request with Cache-Control: no-cache and no If-None-Match, the 200 answer replaces the copy. Run 5 (a bookmark, fresh copy): the same, with Talon-Bookmark: b123 (no-cache always comes with a bookmark).
Runs 6 and 7 (acme/gone, a 404 problem answer, R-IX2, R-AP43): the answer is given as it is, nothing is written, so run 7 asks again. Runs 8 and 9 (contributors/me, a 200 with no-store, R-IX3): never kept, so run 9 asks again.
Run 10 (offline, age 34399 s): the copy at any age, no request, source copy with the time of the meta (R-IX6). Run 11 (offline, no copy): no copy, no request.
Run 12 (acme/slow): no answer, exit 15 and the message of Registry.no_answer. Runs 13 and 14 (acme/low): the answer has lower-case header names (as the real Worker): kept at run 13, used with no request at run 14. Run 15: a route with a query (the key is of the path and the query as sent).
